<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core" xmlns:st="jelly:stapler" xmlns:l="/lib/layout">
  <!--
    Confirm-by-typing-the-name, shared by the Config Set page (delete) and the global list page
    (purge). Both are destructive to whoever is building against the Config Set, so both make the
    operator type its name rather than click Yes.

    CSP migration (Jenkins hosting requirement, see
    https://www.jenkins.io/doc/developer/security/csp/): this fragment used to carry its own
    inline &lt;style&gt;/&lt;script&gt; (CDATA). Both are gone — the identical CSS/JS now lives
    verbatim inside EACH host page's own external index.css/index.js (ConfigTemplatesRootAction,
    ConfigTemplatesJobAction, CommonConfigSetPage), loaded via h.getViewResource(it, ...). It is
    duplicated three times rather than factored into one shared file because this fragment is
    included with `it` bound to whichever HOST page is rendering it (st:include ... it="${it}"),
    so a resource path resolved from `it` always lands next to the CALLER's own index.jelly, never
    a SharedBlocks-relative path. The JS/CSS here never read ${it}, so the three copies are
    byte-identical; keep them that way if this ever changes.
  -->
  <template id="ctsyncConfirmStrings"
            data-cancel-label="${%confirm.cancelLabel}"
            data-name-mismatch="${%confirm.nameMismatch}"/>
</j:jelly>
